      "explained": "Learners applied their full polygon-area toolkit (Lessons 1–7) to the anchoring phenomenon: they decomposed the Kericho seven-sided community plot into standard shapes, calculated the total area, divided it equally into three parts for the Wanjiku, Otieno, and Kosgei farming families, and produced a labelled diagram with a written justification of the fair division, preparing a complete solution for community presentation in Lesson 8."
